    {
      "id": "mother-elen-bright",
      "name": "Mother Elen Bright",
      "species": "Human",
      "gender": "Female",
      "age": 56,
      "occupation": "Temple Priestess",
      "category": "religious",
      "tags": [
        "priestess",
        "mercy",
        "leader"
      ],
      "description": "Familiar face at a local temple; useful, stubborn, and hard to surprise.",
      "biography": "Mother Elen Bright works from a local temple with the stubborn patience of a 56-year-old Human who has already survived harder seasons. She lights a candle for strangers before asking their names, and keeps the prayer beads worn smooth on one side close when tempers rise. Leads temple; suspicious of Quen; mentors Pola. Her private aim is simple: keep the alms kitchen open through winter. Still, she flinches at the thought of faith being twisted into a political weapon. Lately a fresh problem has landed in her lap: Received an anonymous donation of black candles and a warning about 'tower fire'.",
      "personality": "Proud of competence more than praise; lights a candle for strangers before asking their names.",
      "motivation": "Protect her livelihood long enough to keep the alms kitchen open through winter.",
      "secret": "Has not told allies the truth: Received an anonymous donation of black candles and a warning about 'tower fire'.",
      "rumor": "Someone paid Elen to forget a name connected to recent trouble near a local temple.",
      "voice": "Measured human cadence; concrete nouns before adjectives.",
      "appearance": "Work-worn human garb; the prayer beads worn smooth on one side always nearby.",
      "portrait": "modules/townforge/assets/portraits/mother-elen-bright.webp",
