    {
      "id": "brother-caldus",
      "name": "Brother Caldus",
      "species": "Human",
      "gender": "Male",
      "age": 41,
      "occupation": "Temple Archivist",
      "category": "religious",
      "tags": [
        "archive",
        "suspicious",
        "ink"
      ],
      "description": "Familiar face at a temple archive room; useful, stubborn, and hard to surprise.",
      "biography": "Caldus did not plan to become the neighborhood's go-to temple archivist, yet a temple archive room made the choice stick. Now 41, the Human measures success in quiet evenings and unpaid favors returned. He indexes sins as carefully as saints, and keeps the key to a cabinet labeled 'disputed miracles' the way a confessor keeps secrets. Reports to Elen; rivals Quen; uses Finn sometimes. Hope pulls one way—prove Magister Quen's work endangers souls—while caution pulls the other because of magic without doctrine. Copied a page from a restricted folio that matches Quen's latest purchase order.",
      "personality": "Proud of competence more than praise; indexes sins as carefully as saints.",
      "motivation": "Protect his livelihood long enough to prove Magister Quen's work endangers souls.",
      "secret": "Has not told allies the truth: Copied a page from a restricted folio that matches Quen's latest purchase order.",
      "rumor": "Customers claim Caldus knows which doors open after hours—if asked the right way.",
      "voice": "Measured human cadence; concrete nouns before adjectives.",
      "appearance": "Work-worn human garb; the key to a cabinet labeled 'disputed miracles' always nearby.",
