    {
      "id": "sister-pola",
      "name": "Sister Pola",
      "species": "Halfling",
      "gender": "Female",
      "age": 34,
      "occupation": "Alms Keeper",
      "category": "religious",
      "tags": [
        "charity",
        "soup",
        "gentle"
      ],
      "description": "Familiar face at a temple alms porch; useful, stubborn, and hard to surprise.",
      "biography": "Sister Pola works from a temple alms porch with the stubborn patience of a 34-year-old Halfling who has already survived harder seasons. She remembers every hungry face by stew preference, and keeps the ladle polished brighter than the altar plate close when tempers rise. Trained by Elen; feeds Mouse when he looks starved. Her private aim is simple: start a skills school for street children. Still, she flinches at the thought of running out of barley before midwinter. Lately a fresh problem has landed in her lap: A 'beggar' with soft hands asked questions about temple vault schedules.",
      "personality": "Proud of competence more than praise; remembers every hungry face by stew preference.",
      "motivation": "Protect her livelihood long enough to start a skills school for street children.",
      "secret": "Has not told allies the truth: A 'beggar' with soft hands asked questions about temple vault schedules.",
      "rumor": "Pola is said to keep a private list of debts local officials will not touch.",
      "voice": "Measured halfling cadence; concrete nouns before adjectives.",
