    {
      "id": "father-bram",
      "name": "Father Bram",
      "species": "Dwarf",
      "gender": "Male",
      "age": 102,
      "occupation": "Funeral Priest",
      "category": "religious",
      "tags": [
        "burial",
        "solemn",
        "stone"
      ],
      "description": "Bram holds down a quiet funeral chapel with callused competence and open ears.",
      "biography": "Bram learned the hard corners of settlement life by working them as a funeral priest based out of a quiet funeral chapel. At 102, the Dwarf has a map of loyalties written in calluses rather than ink. Day after day he speaks to headstones as neighbors, and the stone chisel blessed for names marks his place in the room. Works with Mol Deeprow; quiet observer of nobles. His north star is to finish the memorial wall for flood victims. The shadow at his heels is unmarked graves becoming a fashion for the wealthy. Paid extra to bury a 'nobody' whose boots were Vale-cobbled.",
      "personality": "Warm with regulars, curt with wasters; speaks to headstones as neighbors.",
      "motivation": "Secure enough ground to finish the memorial wall for flood victims.",
      "secret": "Quietly arranging matters around this problem: Paid extra to bury a 'nobody' whose boots were Vale-cobbled.",
      "rumor": "A smugglers' mark was seen near a quiet funeral chapel on a night Bram worked late.",
      "voice": "Polite public voice; sharper private asides when trust appears.",
      "appearance": "Looks like someone who sleeps lightly; distinctive detail is the stone chisel blessed for names.",
      "portrait": "modules/townforge/assets/portraits/father-bram.webp",
