    {
      "id": "acolyte-ren",
      "name": "Ren Candlemark",
      "species": "Human",
      "gender": "Male",
      "age": 18,
      "occupation": "Acolyte",
      "category": "religious",
      "tags": [
        "acolyte",
        "earnest",
        "bells"
      ],
      "description": "Local acolyte whose days orbit temple aisles before dawn and small lasting loyalties.",
      "biography": "Before dawn, Ren is already at temple aisles before dawn, working as a acolyte with yesterday's work still on his fingers. The habit everyone notices is simple: he practices sermons to empty pews. Close by sits his prized the taper box with one lucky stub, a small anchor in a loud settlement. Earnest junior under Elen and Caldus. He wants to be trusted to hold the dawn service alone. He fears failing his vows by gossiping more than open confrontation. A useful adventure hook trails him: Saw Brother Caldus meet a cloaked figure behind the charnel hedge.",
      "personality": "Dry humor over a careful heart; practices sermons to empty pews.",
      "motivation": "Finish one honest plan: be trusted to hold the dawn service alone.",
      "secret": "Keeps proof related to a problem—Saw Brother Caldus meet a cloaked figure behind the charnel hedge.",
      "rumor": "Someone paid Ren to forget a name connected to recent trouble near temple aisles before dawn.",
      "voice": "Storyteller rhythm even when discussing ledgers or latches.",
      "appearance": "Human features shaped by work at temple aisles before dawn; watch for the taper box with one lucky stub.",
