    {
      "id": "seer-ivra",
      "name": "Ivra Glass-Eye",
      "species": "Tiefling",
      "gender": "Female",
      "age": 39,
      "occupation": "Oracle",
      "category": "religious",
      "tags": [
        "oracle",
        "visions",
        "controversial"
      ],
      "description": "Familiar face at a curtained reading chamber; useful, stubborn, and hard to surprise.",
      "biography": "Some locals swear Ivra was born mid-shift at a curtained reading chamber; the truth is only slightly less devoted. This tiefling oracle, now 39, treats competence like courtesy. She covers her glass eye when the visions itch, never far from the bowl of river stones for casting. Controversial; Rold rents her the room; Elen half-believes her. Ask what she wants and she names it plainly: warn the town of a real fire before it happens. Ask what she dreads and the answer is being used as a party trick by nobles. Then comes the fresh problem—Predicted 'iron in grain and blood in cloaks' a week before Mira's stool seven mystery.",
      "personality": "Proud of competence more than praise; covers her glass eye when the visions itch.",
      "motivation": "Protect her livelihood long enough to warn the town of a real fire before it happens.",
