      "description": "A cloister monk rooted at a cloister garden, known for how he answers questions with another hour of weeding.",
      "biography": "Sol Quietstep's reputation as a cloister monk was built one careful errand at a time around a cloister garden. Age 44 sits lightly on this Human, except when old debts creak. Watch long enough and you will see that he answers questions with another hour of weeding. The kneeling pad stuffed with lavender is part tool, part talisman. Shares garden knowledge with Yara; peaceful counterweight to Caldus. He would trade sleep to teach silence as a craft, not a punishment, yet stays wary of violence entering sacred quiet. Current spark: Found chalk sigils under the cloister bench matching Nym's survey marks.",
      "personality": "Steady and sharp-eyed; answers questions with another hour of weeding.",
      "motivation": "To teach silence as a craft, not a punishment, even while fearing violence entering sacred quiet.",
