        "comfort"
      ],
      "description": "The guard chaplain people recommend when they actually want the job finished.",
      "biography": "Dorr did not plan to become the neighborhood's go-to guard chaplain, yet a small chapel near the barracks made the choice stick. Now 37, the Half-Orc measures success in quiet evenings and unpaid favors returned. He sits with shaking guards until their hands still, and keeps the portable altar cloth stained with polish oil the way a confessor keeps secrets. Chaplain to Serra's guards. Hope pulls one way—keep Serra's watch human when the case hardens—while caution pulls the other because of blessing a raid that kills the wrong people. Heard Dorn admit he almost killed Bask—and wants penance, not praise.",
      "personality": "Soft-spoken until principles are poked; sits with shaking guards until their hands still.",
      "motivation": "Turn today's scrapes into tomorrow's chance to keep Serra's watch human when the case hardens.",
      "secret": "Night thoughts keep returning to blessing a raid that kills the wrong people, especially since: Heard Dorn admit he almost killed Bask—and wants penance, not praise.",
      "rumor": "Dorr is said to keep a private list of debts local officials will not touch.",
      "voice": "Quick local diction, then sudden silences that mean more than words.",
